+# NEVERMERGE — one Windows worker-flight witness
+
+This evidence-only branch starts at `79cdb85d6ab8a58dde5d474e254cffa027735c51`. It must never be merged or opened as an application/release PR. Its replacement `.github/workflows/full-ci.yml` is a diagnostic `workflow_dispatch` on this branch only, not Full CI qualification. No default/main source, test metric, product, dependency, golden, sample, threshold or native capability changes.
+
+The original Windows browser1 failure remains failed: YAML quick flight gaps98/89/28/1ms exceeded40% of its159ms main-thread reference. The same-code Mac witness passed and exposed an endpoint/MO-close attribution bias, but did not establish the Windows89ms cause. This one Windows witness retains the original metric and assertion; it is neither a blind retry nor a metric repair.
+
+The portable diagnostic differs from accepted `0bf63aa3fc13dfe4bcbd41ec5c685fec41e0b74b985e6d0ac4a62c130e185cb2` only in its three helper imports and owned output location. Exact inverse bindings are in `source-bindings.json`. The entire recorder, four quick/twelve paced edits, three formats/two patterns, one round, environment controls and all verdict gates remain unchanged. All9 relevant source/helper files equal79 (and0fe). The four generated browser assets must match the exact failed Windows artifact hashes before browser activation. The runner's base79 tree/path allowlist prevents unrelated committed changes; clean Git and before/between/after source/assets/ALL regular dist-file inventories prevent hidden local changes.
+
+The single20-minute windows-latest job uses the existing pinned checkout/setup-workspace/upload actions, Node24.22.2, pnpm10.33.2, lock-pinned Playwright1.65.0/Chromium158.0.8127.18, normal maintained package/playground builds and one Chromium install. `fetch-depth:2` provides the single reviewed source commit and its required first parent79 for exact tree comparison, without retrieving historical evidence archives. No arbitrary workflow inputs, secrets, account changes, Office or retry loop. Root may dispatch once only after source review and normal push of this exact evidence commit.
+
+Execution is one fixed `node docs/evidence/worker-flight-witness/run.mjs`. After authority/assets checks, it first invokes the separate Office-free `native-controls.mjs` for the sole maintained `node --test scripts/native-acceptance/reference-name-snapshot.test.mjs`, preserving the32 actual managed startup/Save/adapter controls and original outcomes. It does not run the separate already-qualified startup file. It then runs the one normal portable browser diagnostic. These independent outcomes are both retained; either failure leaves the overall diagnostic failed. An initial source/asset prerequisite failure starts neither child; drift after the native controls holds the browser witness. No live PowerPoint, process enumeration, native document edits or new native evidence is requested.
+
+Browser child environment removes inherited OPF overrides and Node preloads/donor resolution, then explicitly binds CI=true/LIMIT100/ROUNDS1/COMPAREtrue/workerOfffalse/BURN0/SLOW0/Chromium/CPU1/nativeWindows keymap. Actual versions/parameters and Git HEAD are recorded, not assumed. Outer controls120-second/browser360-second caps leave room for always-upload within the20-minute job, without altering any original per-wait deadline. All files, child stdout/stderr/exit/error and raw report are under `artifacts/worker-flight-witness/` and uploaded on `always()`. Child startup errors remain in the outer receipt/log even when the diagnostic's pre-try startup cannot fill originalFailure. Existing original assertions are never replaced by diagnostic success; missing evidence, drift or any child RED makes the wrapper fail. A Windows pass is a new scoped observation, not retrospective proof that the first failure was noise or physical-device fidelity.
+
+SOURCE ONLY: no installation, import, syntax check, build, test, browser, push or dispatch by the author at preparation. Root and independent peer review precede the single workflow assignment. The prior Mac witness is not repeated; no BURN/worker-off fault control is part of this first Windows run.
